# Zoho and data integrity

Initial Zoho integration is **READ ONLY**. Do not add CRM write permissions until read/analysis behaviour is proven.

Never invent Zoho API endpoints or schema. Verify against current official Zoho CRM v8 docs before implementation. UI-visible data is not automatically available via API.

Preserve source IDs. Separate verified, imported, and AI-inferred data, with source, confidence, and last-verified date. Never silently overwrite verified CRM data with AI output.

Identity resolution is deterministic first (normalised email, domain, company identifiers, normalised name, existing Zoho relationships, later Portal Genie account/user IDs). Do not auto-merge uncertain identities; flag them for review.

AI summaries must never replace source records. Recommendations must be explainable with evidence. Assumptions must not be presented as verified facts.
